{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/EnvironmentValues"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/EnvironmentValues\/refresh"},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI17EnvironmentValuesV7refreshAA13RefreshActionVSgvp","modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"refresh"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"RefreshAction","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI13RefreshActionV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"role":"symbol","extendedModule":"OpenSwiftUI","title":"refresh","roleHeading":"Instance Property"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"refresh"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI13RefreshActionV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"RefreshAction","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/RefreshAction"},{"kind":"text","text":"? { "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"set"},{"kind":"text","text":" }"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When this environment value contains an instance of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/RefreshAction"},{"text":" structure, certain built-in views in the corresponding","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Environment"},{"text":" begin offering a refresh capability. They apply the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instance’s handler to any refresh operation that the user initiates.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"By default, the environment value is ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", but you can use the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"View\/refreshable(action:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" modifier to create and store a new","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"refresh action that uses the handler that you specify:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["List(mailbox.conversations) { conversation in","    ConversationCell(conversation)","}",".refreshable {","    await mailbox.fetch()","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"On iOS and iPadOS, the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"List"},{"text":" in the example above offers a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pull to refresh gesture because it detects the refresh action. When","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the user drags the list down and releases, the list calls the action’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"handler. Because SwiftUI declares the handler as asynchronous, it can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"safely make long-running asynchronous calls, like fetching network data.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Refreshing-Custom-Views","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Refreshing Custom Views"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can also offer refresh capability in your custom views."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Read the "},{"code":"refresh","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" environment value to get the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/RefreshAction"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instance for a given "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Environment"},{"type":"text","text":". If you find"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a non-"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" value, change your view’s appearance or behavior to offer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the refresh to the user, and call the instance to conduct the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"refresh. You can call the refresh instance directly because it defines"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/RefreshAction\/callAsFunction()"},{"type":"text","text":" method that Swift calls"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when you call the instance:"}]},{"code":["struct RefreshableView: View {","    @Environment(\\.refresh) private var refresh","","    var body: some View {","        Button(\"Refresh\") {","            Task {","                await refresh?()","            }","        }","        .disabled(refresh == nil)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Be sure to call the handler asynchronously by preceding it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"text":". Because the call is asynchronous, you can use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its lifetime to indicate progress to the user. For example,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"you can reveal an indeterminate ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProgressView"},{"text":" before","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"calling the handler, and hide it when the handler completes.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If your code isn’t already in an asynchronous context, create a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/Swift\/Task"},{"type":"text","text":" for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"method to run in. If you do this, consider adding a way for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"user to cancel the task. For more information, see"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/docs.swift.org\/swift-book\/LanguageGuide\/Concurrency.html","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Swift Programming Language"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A refresh action stored in a view’s environment."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/environmentvalues\/refresh"]}],"references":{"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/Environment":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Environment"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/environment","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A property wrapper that reads a value from a view’s environment."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"Environment","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Environment"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Environment"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/RefreshAction":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/RefreshAction","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RefreshAction","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RefreshAction","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"An action that initiates a refresh operation.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/refreshaction","title":"RefreshAction","kind":"symbol"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/EnvironmentValues":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"OpenSwiftUI exposes a collection of values to your app’s views in an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EnvironmentValues"},{"text":" structure. To read a value from the structure,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"declare a property using the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Environment","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" property wrapper and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specify the value’s key path. For example, you can read the current locale:","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EnvironmentValues","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/EnvironmentValues","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EnvironmentValues","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"EnvironmentValues","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/environmentvalues"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI":{"title":"OpenSwiftUI","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"https://docs.swift.org/swift-book/LanguageGuide/Concurrency.html":{"type":"link","title":"Concurrency","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Concurrency","type":"text"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/docs.swift.org\/swift-book\/LanguageGuide\/Concurrency.html","url":"https:\/\/docs.swift.org\/swift-book\/LanguageGuide\/Concurrency.html"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/RefreshAction/callAsFunction()":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/refreshaction\/callasfunction()","title":"callAsFunction()","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Initiates a refresh action.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/RefreshAction\/callAsFunction()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"callAsFunction"},{"kind":"text","text":"() "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"}]},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/EnvironmentValues/refresh":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/environmentvalues\/refresh","title":"refresh","abstract":[{"text":"A refresh action stored in a view’s environment.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/EnvironmentValues\/refresh","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"refresh","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RefreshAction","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI13RefreshActionV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]}}}